     <div style="background: #fff;
                    width: 90%;
                    margin-right: auto;
                    margin-left: auto;">
                   Dear {!Contact.FirstName}, <br /><br />

<b>Student ID: {!Contact.EMPLID__c}</b><br /><br />

Thank you for submitting your application for graduation from Arizona State University. At this time, <b>your application has been denied</b> for the following reason(s): <br /><br />

<ul>
	<li>You have not reached candidacy. Once you have reached candidacy you may reapply for graduation with no additional fee.</li> <br /><br />

	<li>Your iPOS (Plan of Study) indicates that you have exceeded your graduation deadline. You must submit a petition requesting a time limit extension for a Graduate College decision. If this petition is approved you will need to reapply for graduation with no additional fee. </li><br /><br />

       <li>Your iPOS (Plan of Study) GPA, Overall Graduate (500 level courses and above) GPA or Cumulative GPA is below 3.00. Graduate College requires that students maintain a minimum 3.00 GPA on all GPAs (iPOS, Overall Graduate and Cumulative) to graduate. Please contact your academic unit staff/advisor to review your options and create a plan of action. Once you have communicated with your academic unit, please e-mail the Graduation Office with an update on your status. To calculate your GPA please visit <a href="https://students.asu.edu/gpa-calculator">https://students.asu.edu/gpa-calculator</a>.</li> <br /><br />

	<li>Your iPOS (Plan of Study) has not been approved by Graduate College. Your iPOS must be approved by Graduate College by the  <a href="https://students.asu.edu/academic-calendar">graduation conferral date.</a> Once your iPOS has been approved you can reapply for graduation with no additional fee.</li><br /><br />

	<li>You are not registered for the semester in which you have applied for graduation. Graduate College requires that all graduate students be enrolled in <b><u>at least </b></u>one graduate level credit hour in the semester they are graduating. </li> <br /><br />
</ul>

For more information on ASU Graduate Policies and Procedures please visit <a href="https://graduate.asu.edu/policies-procedures">https://graduate.asu.edu/policies-procedures</a>.<br /><br />

Please contact your department for guidance if you have questions. Your academic unit staff have been copied on this email for reference. <br /><br />


Sincerely, <br />

{!Case.OwnerFullName}<br /><br/>

        <div style="color:#990033;font-family: Arial, Helvetica !important;">
                        <b>Graduation<br />
                        University Registrar Services</b><br />
